============================================================

1. HELVANTHOR LOWER MARKET — POV Dusty
- Wet slate sky, rotting market. Dusty (hooded, rags, filthy, stinks) guards Old Tobin's bread stall for pay in bread. Bends his height down under the awning.
- Two city watchmen (red tabards faded pink) are useless: one eats a stolen apple, one ogles a washerwoman.
- An elf arrives with two Mythrandis guards (plate, spears, blue shields with a white tower). Tobin names the academy. The elf taps cups, pots and scales, muttering about thinness and walls: she's testing resonance.
- Dusty deters three thieves with his candle-sized flame (orange flame, black haze around his fingers, hairline silver edge):
  a) small boy (6-7): shown the flame, "Please don't." He runs.
  b) teen with boil and cudgel: flame held at his eye. He returns the loaves and spits.
  c) plague-sick man (sores, cough): refuses to stop, so Dusty BURNS the back of his hand. He falls into the gutter, the loaf is lost, he limps off sobbing. Dusty wipes his hand after.
- The elf watches, fixed on Dusty's fist. Dusty turns his shoulder to her.
- Noon bell. Tobin pays THREE loaves ("For the sick one. That was ugly work.").

2. THE GREYS — POV Dusty
- The slum sits in a low bowl over a buried river: rotten tenements, black water, huddled families watching the bread.
- Ambush by 10+ children (none older than 12) led by a boy with a split lip and a missing ear. Dusty says "I'm sorry. I can't."
- Brutal fight. Flame in a girl's mouth, flame across a boy's eyes (blinding him), knee, elbow, nose broken. He takes a rock to the cheekbone, a board across the back, a rock to the thigh. A girl steals ONE loaf. Two loaves left. "Please. Go home." They scatter; the blinded are led away.
- His mana stays full. His body is spent.
- "Halt!" The guards arrive: HOLT (big, heavy jaw, leads with his spear) and PELL (younger, lean, thin mouth, contemptuous: "street filth").
- The elf, VALIA VELANTHUS, pushes the spear aside, asks for the onlookers to be moved back ("they're all breathing, it's very loud"), and backs Dusty against a wall. She's shorter (head at his chin). She smells of rain and old paper.
- He withholds his name until she frames her guards as the same as him guarding Tobin. Then: "Dusty."
- She's fixated on the COLOR (black, silver edge), not the size. She counted 23 lights. He has never run out. Longest hold: "All night" (the memory of warming Rinnie).
- She mutters a plan (Headmaster always says yes, a leftover lottery spot, classes). Offer: "How would you like to go to a magic school?"
- He refuses: other responsibilities. She offers to talk to his parents. He tells her, flatly, that the city guard seals off coughing-sickness streets and burns them with people inside; his parents died that way EIGHT YEARS AGO. Valia freezes, then is outraged. Pell looks at his boots.
- "My sister is sick." Rinnie, 12, sick a long time, undiagnosed. "I won't leave her."
- Valia offers a room for Rinnie in AETHRES (the city at the mainland end of the bridge), visits on rest days, and academy healers. Dusty searches the offer for the hook. He pictures an island full of Pells.
- Clincher: "You could learn it yourself." Healing is about holding mana steady, not quantity, and he never stops. He could heal Rinnie with his own hands.
- "I'll come." Valia: "New travelers!" She asks to meet Rinnie. Dusty's last line: "Will her room have a window? A window for the sun?"

3. DEVOUT QUARTER / WAY STATION, HELVANTHOR — POV Dusty
- Next morning. Dusty is scrubbed and in new brown linen and real boots (Valia dragged a tailor out of bed). Rinnie has a white cotton gown and a thick black hooded cloak, plus her frayed BLUE RIBBON (Dusty hauled crates two days to buy it the winter she turned eight). Dusty carries her in his arms.
- The cathedral is white and gold-tipped. Cream-robed priests, censers of cedar and honey.
- SAINTESS SIGHTING: a girl about Rinnie's age, white silk, near-white gold hair, eyes down, led BY THE WRIST by an ancient hunched priest with a black staff, inside a hollow square of 8 guards in white-and-gold enamel. Priests bow and touch two fingers to their lips. Rinnie: "She looks tired."
- Way Station: a windowless white marble dome with bronze doors, guarded by Church guards in white enamel. Valia's pocket search turns up a pencil stub, notes, a spiral copper wire, a dried leaf, and a clapperless brass bell. Holt: "Left side, my lady. Inside." The papers carry a white-tower seal.
- The crystal: the size of three horses, floating over a black marble platform, turning slowly and scattering light. Four gray-robed mages power it. Nobles (one woman with a lace handkerchief who sneers at the siblings) depart for CALVENNE. The crystal RINGS like a great bell when it fires.
- Valia's lore: the Church builds and runs Way Stations. Mages GROW the crystals from a thumbnail seed stone over decades of daily mana; each use wears it until it cracks. Very expensive. Rinnie: "Did they borrow it from a giant?" Pell snorts; Dusty stares him down.
- Dusty squeezes Rinnie too hard on the platform and apologizes. Rinnie: "You're squishing the cloak. It's new."
- Valia reassures them ("It sounds lovely from the inside"). Her hand lingers on Dusty's shoulder. She squeezes once, wordless.

4. ARRIVAL (DUKE'S TOWN) — POV Dusty
- Sunset; it was morning in Helvanthor (time-zone shift). A clean, rich town: honey brick, flower boxes, a Way Station dome plus a small cathedral, a DUKE'S manor on a rise with a blue banner. The town is unnamed.
- A happy market: a fiddle, a freckled flower girl swatting a guard with a daisy. Dusty still scans hands and alleys; nobody is starving.
- MAIDS appear silently inside the group's circle: GWENITH and MAEDELYN. Holt and Pell flinch hard; Valia yelps.
  - Gwenith: shorter, light brown high ponytail, hazel eyes, dimples, warm, gushing. Shushes Rinnie with a finger to her lips; Rinnie mirrors it.
  - Maedelyn: taller, dark blue straight hair, deep blue kohl-lined eyes, composed, clipped.
- Maedelyn: three rooms at the GILDED PHEASANT, supplies packed, depart at first light. Maedelyn says FOUR days' ride.
- Dusty asks what arrangements there are for Rinnie, who can't ride. Valia panics and babbles her whole backstory of the day. Dusty: "She can ride with me." Maedelyn has already arranged a horse for Dusty plus a covered pony cart with cushions, a roof, and side panels that open. Dusty and Rinnie both bow in thanks. Gwenith: "Can we keep them?"

5. GILDED PHEASANT SUPPER + WOMEN'S ROOM — POV VALIA (first POV switch)
- Valia listens to the room: floorboard pitch, fork tapping. Holt clears his throat.
- Dusty won't eat and hovers over Rinnie's bites. Rinnie: "I have to eat slow... or it all comes back up."
- Holt and Pell exchange contemptuous looks, which Valia notices. She lectures Dusty clumsily, then plainly: "Your sister is in better hands right now than yours. You look like a skeleton. Eat." Rinnie also asks him to take care of himself, "For me." Gwenith offers to count Rinnie's bites.
- Dusty's brief crooked smile. He eats FIVE plates, his eyes wet. Rinnie counts them aloud. Later Rinnie orders him to bed ("Bed."). He dips his head to Valia at the door.
- Women's room: Valia's FATHER'S BROWN ROBE lies folded at the foot of her bed (patched elbows). She doesn't look at it.
- Rinnie questions Gwenith (how to become a maid; "Some are asked. Some ask."; "Very important tea"; "Your shoes didn't make any noise"; "Can I become one?"). Maedelyn cuts in with the maxim: "All actions must be with Beauty, Elegance, and Dignity above all else." LORE: "Long ago, the Maids served a monster. When he died, we chose to serve the academy instead." Valia has never heard a Maid say that much in forty years.
- Rinnie questions Valia: research = sound, whether mana can shake air without a bell. Rinnie: "Like the crystal. It rang." Valia: nobody ever gets that. Forty years. Boyfriend? No (flustered). Friends? "Not many." Valia pictures the empty seats by her window seat in the dining hall. Maedelyn defends her: "Most of the faculty could not keep pace with her."
- Rinnie: "You're his first friend." He spent everything on her. "I'm glad I don't have to be that anymore. Something he has to carry." She asks Valia to look after him. VALIA PROMISES (make him eat and sleep).
- Maids whisper-argue in the dark; Maedelyn: "—ask permission first." Valia falls asleep hearing the grate tick like a distant bell.

6. THE ROAD — POV Dusty
- Hot, dusty wheat fields. Dusty's first time on a horse (brown mare). Rinnie sleeps in Gwenith's lap in the cart, paying for yesterday.
- Dusty asks why the Way Station didn't send them closer. Pell snorts. Valia: nobody should be shamed for asking. Dusty to Pell, pleasantly: "Guards should spend more time guarding, and less time sharing their opinions."
- Holt and Pell lower their spears and charge. Maedelyn is instantly across the road (she was at the head of the column a moment before). Gwenith stands in the cart, dimples gone. Maedelyn: the guards' duty is protection, "not their correction"; protecting students is the Maid Corps' duty too, "From any threat." The guards fall back 30 paces. Pell trembles, and Holt won't face her. Dusty files it with the silent shoes.
- Valia is shaken. Maedelyn comforts her ("You are quite safe"). Valia then tells Dusty to report any guard trouble to her.
- "Valia. Please. Just Valia."
- LORE (Valia): there are no nations, kingdoms, or cities under a crown within 100 miles around the lake, because the academy forbids it. The Church is a power, so no Way Station nearby; everyone rides the last stretch ("Everyone gets dusty"). Someone tried to build there long ago; nobody talks about what happened. Neutrality holds because every ruler attended Mythrandis and they write to classmates for decades, and because nobody wants the faculty or the Headmaster cross with them. It prevents wars.
- Dusty: Helvanthor has been at war with THE NORTH since he was small. Valia has no answer ("Nothing's perfect").
- "How will you get me in? ... I'm no one." Valia: "You're very important. To Rinnie. And to me." She backpedals, mortified.
- PITY LOTTERY (her account): 4-5k students, just over 300 non-noble, admitted by talent or skill, noble sponsorship, or random clergy picks from villages. Dusty fits none. "You have me!" She'll ask Headmaster ANTONAEZ, "something like my sponsor... Ever since—" She freezes (grief tell). Dusty recognizes the stillness from Rinnie.
- Valia is sure Antonaez will say yes, especially for a mana study. Dusty: "Then I'll be your lab rat." She babbles about resonance tests: tuning fork, copper wire, iron-post rig, teeth buzzing, hair standing up.
- Dusty SMILES. "I don't think you'd hurt me, Valia." (First time he uses her name.) He'll help with anything as long as Rinnie is looked after. She promises Rinnie will be safe.

7. AETHRES — POV Dusty
- The trip actually took FIVE days on the road. Rinnie twice rode on the mare with Dusty, laughing, and paid for it both times; Maedelyn called early halts unasked.
- A tent city of noble camps, with banners (golden stag on green, three silver fish on blue, red hand gripping a sword), starts a mile out. 40-ft gray walls, square towers, portcullis. The city is packed; Mythrandis-blue guards stand on every corner. Pale island towers are visible over the rooftops, rising from the water.
- Bridge timing (Valia): returning students cross first and get a day to settle; first years cross the day after. Valia recites the charter: the crossing is "the first and most sacred tradition... you walk across alone... an equal among equals."
- Dusty laughs ("You said it like you read it from a book." / "I did... It's in the charter. It's a good line."). His rebuttal: a king's son is still a king's son on the other side, and he's still from the Greys. Valia concedes, then vows to pay him "the right kind of attention... you'll feel like a king's son." Dusty, watching Rinnie point at a monkey with a faint rose in her cheeks, wipes his eyes: "You already do." Valia goes scarlet.
- Inn: four stories, whitewashed, green shutters, SILVER SWAN sign (the name isn't given beyond the sign). Dusty says there won't be rooms. Maedelyn: "The Maid Corps always has a room, young man." Dusty: fear, respect, or gratitude? Maedelyn doesn't answer until inside, after a nod exchanged with the barrel-broad matron: "Many fear us. Some are grateful. But most respect us." Dusty: "I'm one of the grateful ones." Maedelyn almost smiles.
- Top-floor room: four beds, two windows. Rinnie gets the sunny bed by the window (this pays off his window question).
- Valia dismisses Holt and Pell. They bow deeply to the MAIDS, not her ("It was an honor"), and flee.
- Gwenith presses Maedelyn: "You have to talk to them. About the permission. You promised." Maedelyn: "Today."
- Valia leaves to see the Headmaster tonight, to arrange Rinnie's room, healers, and enrollment. Maedelyn goes with her. Gwenith stays with the siblings. Dusty is told to stay put.
- END: Gwenith mends and hums. Dusty holds Rinnie's cold hand as she sleeps in the sun.

8. SILVER SWAN, NEXT DAY — POV Dusty
- A day passes. Maedelyn returns with Valia and tells Gwenith: "You have permission." Gwenith hugs Rinnie ("my little sparrow", "sweet pea"). Explanation: Gwenith and Maedelyn are the Maids who look after Valia (they take turns in her lab: tea, lunch, books, bedtime). Rinnie is now "Lady Valia's guest," so she falls under them. "So I asked Maedelyn to ask. And they said yes." WHO "they" are is still unstated.
- Gwenith will care for Rinnie daily (brush her hair, count bites, soft bread). Dusty bows: "Thank you, ma'am." Gwenith: "don't ma'am me."
- Valia: the Headmaster approved Dusty as a LATE LOTTERY ADDITION ("the very last one"); he's being put into classes. Antonaez "sat very still" and SIGHED at her TWICE; she's annoyed he was annoyed. "He always says yes."
- Dusty can't read the papers (neat slanted hand) but knows the seal. Feels out of place.
- Valia: "you'll have a tutor for letters if you need one, you do need one." First years walk the bridge IN FOUR DAYS. She panics: uniform (blazer, tie, slacks, boots), comb, soap, tooth powder, razor, trunk. Maedelyn: "I will see to it."
- Maedelyn: Valia must return to the academy TONIGHT (faculty meet before the crossing; she missed the last two) and "You cannot play favorites." Valia: "I'm extremely fair." Maedelyn's eyebrow.
- Valia hugs Rinnie ("You're in good hands"), then an awkward hug with Dusty (Rinnie: "Oh, for— Dusty."). "Since the fire, only Rinnie had ever reached for him like that." Valia: "You're very tall." Flustered, fixes her cloak badly. "I'll see you on the island. Not specially. Just normally. The normal amount." Maedelyn to Dusty: "Young man." / "Ma'am."
- Rinnie's serious face (their MOTHER'S face): study properly, Gwenith has her now, but visit EVERY REST DAY. Dusty: "I've still got four days." Ends on the academy across the lake.

9. THE BRIDGE / FIRST DAY ON THE ISLAND — POV Dusty
- Mid-morning, four days later. A barber (arranged by Maedelyn) trimmed Dusty's hair and slicked it back with CEDAR OIL. Uniform: black slacks, black undershirt, DEEP BLUE SILK TIE (Gwenith knotted it), DARK NAVY WOOL BLAZER with the white tower in silver thread, black boots stiff at the ankles. First clothes ever made to fit him; he keeps tugging the cuffs.
- Plaza before the bridge: hundreds of rich families in silk, farewells in waves. Trunks on iron-shod wheels and handcarts. Dusty spots 4-5 poor students (sun-browned, plain, cotton socks, battered trunk, canvas bag).
- RINNIE'S HOUSE in Aethres: narrow honey-brick house on the rise above the market, three stories, red geraniums; Gwenith found and furnished it in two days; an academy healer comes each morning. Rinnie's window: third floor, left, beneath the eave. Empty; she's asleep (overdid it touching everything, painted birds on her ceiling).
- GWENITH in the crowd holding RINNIE'S BLUE RIBBON. A nod, then gone. Dusty fights tears and crosses.
- Bridge: pale gray stone, room for four carriages, carved-vine parapets, a Guard every 50 paces. Long walk; the academy grows until "the towers had swallowed the sky."
- Arrival court: dozens of Maids sort students into groups of 30. Dusty's Maid: MAID ORIEL (tall, copper-red hair, heavy kohl, GRAY eyes). Route: left at the bronze-fish fountain, right under the carved-owl arch. White-flagstone courtyard ringed by lime trees.
- Oriel's speech: schedule (breakfast 7, first class 8, lunch noon, classes end 3, tea 4, dinner 6, curfew 10 "not a suggestion"); schedules and rooms delivered by the Maid Corps, "You will not ask who decided them. You will not ask to trade them." Girl in gold: "And if my room is unsuitable?" / "It will not be." Equality line. (See continuity flags re: Oriel reciting the Maids' creed.)
- The tour is described in general terms only: libraries three stories high, lecture halls, dining halls, practice yard, gardens, flawless statues. Dusty looks for the rot and finds none. Two brothers in green in different groups stop dead, and the Maids move them on. Seen in passing: a girl in violet with a BLACK SASH (a prefect) and a young man in a WHITE SHAWL (Council President) with a following. Neither is named.
- Dorm: northern dormitories, THIRD hall, FOURTH floor, SEVENTH door on the left. Brass plate: "DUSTY" (no family name). Room: south window, feather bed, blue wool blanket, dark oak desk (lamp, paper, ink), armoire with brass hooks, white-tiled washroom (basin, pitcher, copper tub).
- MEMORY: at 6-7 he lived in two rooms above a COOPER'S SHOP in the lower city (cracked window, smoking stove, leaking roof over the flour corner). Rinnie as a baby in a rag-lined crate. His FATHER MENDED BOOTS and sang off-key. Rent went up, they fell into the Greys, then the coughing came "with the guards close behind it."
- The four o'clock bell. He goes down to tea alone. "He'd eaten alone before."

10. FIRST DAY OF CLASSES — POV Dusty (internal *** breaks)
- INTRO TO MAGIC: PROFESSOR BRANNOCH (bigger than Dusty, russet square-cut beard, huge forearms, booming "GOOD MORNING!", snaps chalk). ~50 students. The three alignments: martial (inward, NO glow), elemental (outward, hands glow, color unique), healing (into others, hands glow, hardest). You don't choose; you're born leaning one way. "Blended. We'll fight over you in the faculty lounge." Reserves: well, pond, lake, ocean ("Those ones, you do not annoy"). Empty means legs go, eyes go, you wake in the Solarium. Refill with sleep and food in about a day. "Manage it."
- Dusty writes HEALING, then ASK VALIA (fire is elemental; is he healing?). He has NEVER run out: held the flame all night for years, 23 lights in one morning plus the Greys fight. Keeps quiet. "only a candle that had never guttered out."
- DUSTY'S LITERACY: barely reads; writes in square block letters learned from shop signs, spells by sound. Keeps a running "ASK VALIA" list at the back of his notebook (healing vs fire, potions and why, a tutor).
- HISTORY OF THE WORLD: stooped old lecturer (unnamed) reading from a ledger. Vague. Dusty fills four pages and understands half.
- MAGICAL APPLICATION: about 200 students (three times Brannoch's), stone half-bowl with a sand pit. PROFESSOR VENN: elf, silver hair cropped close, charcoal robes, soft voice that carries, NO glow from her hands (mastery). Breathing, finding the warmth beneath the breastbone, coaxing it to the hands. The hall lights up in colors; Dusty keeps his flame hidden. Next class: alignment testing, then placement into alignment classes. A boy in crimson with a signet ring says his tutors confirmed him elemental/fire at eight. Venn: all will be tested, "Not according to what your tutors told your mother."
- LUNCH: eats alone, the others moving four feet away. Remembers Valia's "You look like a skeleton. Eat." Five plates; girls across the aisle count them.
- POTIONS: FOUNDATIONS: mixed years, smoky vaulted room. Dusty doesn't know why he's enrolled (added to the Valia list). AURIEL LANDSDON waves him over ("Tall one!"). She's surrounded by EMPTY STOOLS (3 left, 2 right) in a packed room; girls choose to stand. Auriel: honey-gold hair loose to her hips, amber/gold eyes, round soft face, full cheeks, short, curvy, WHITE BLAZER, crooked RED SILK SASH with gold thread. Fast, bright questions. Dusty: "Just Dusty," from Helvanthor, hoping for healing. Auriel: "Healing! That's the best one." Don't tell Brannoch, or push-ups.
- PROFESSOR MOTTRAM (thin, gray, scorched leather apron, spectacles pushed into iron-gray frizz, yellow-brown stained fingers). Auriel: "She's wonderful. She's terrifying." Mana restorative (blue): fills about a third, headache, three a day means vomiting. Wound draught (rust red): cuts and muscle only. Every potion does one thing. The year: fever tinctures, sleeping draughts, antidotes per poison, burn salves, bruise poultices, COUGHWORT (lung tonic). Dusty underlines lungs, fevers, weakness of the blood for Rinnie (she coughs at night, cold hands).
- Auriel draws Brannoch doing push-ups in her margin. After class: a half-second hesitation, hand half-reaching, then the tea invite. Dusty: "Yes. I'd like that." She lights up. "The blue courtyard, the one with the swan statue... the good cakes go first!" She runs off before giving directions. The room goes quiet and whispers; Dusty wonders if tea with an upperclassman is taboo.

11. SEARCHING FOR THE BLUE COURTYARD — POV Dusty
- Wanders courtyards (yellow stone and oak, gray and lavender, green marble, red brick, white, rearing bronze horse, woman with scales, carp pond). Plans to study tonight, sounding out words. Wants a tutor but Valia has done enough. Will give her the whole list once, when she calls him to her EAST WING lab; doesn't know when.
- Four o'clock bell. Tea everywhere: canopies, tiered cakes, blankets, a boy in gold holding court under wisteria. A MAID at every courtyard, watching. Dusty marvels at the logistics and resents the ritual. Rinnie had relayed Gwenith's "very important tea."
- Frustration builds: can't read, the empty stools, girls counting plates, missing Rinnie, and the noble boys with signet rings whose fathers could have signed the order to burn the sick. He presses it down.
- Half-past-four bell (single note): tea ends, bows and curtseys, Maids collect cups. Guilt. Aloud: "Why would a girl like that even want to have tea with me?"
- A NAVY BLUE PASSAGE he'd walked past twice leads to a small navy-walled courtyard: a stone SWAN carved so fine light glows through the wing edges, water bubbling beneath its breast into a channel, tall rows of fat WHITE ROSES in clusters of 3-4. A curved concrete bench and table: teapot under a cozy, TWO CUPS (one poured, one clean and dry), a ring of iced cakes, one of each color.
- Auriel alone, hands over her face, crying silently. Dusty's anger drains. SCENE SPLIT HERE.

12. THE SWAN COURTYARD — POV Dusty
- Dusty clears his throat. Auriel startles and blames the roses. Dusty turns his back and smells the roses to give her cover. She names them MOONSILK (brought from the eastern beds) and says they smell of honey, rain, and clean sheets. Dusty: "They smell like honey."
- He bows and apologizes; he walked past the passage twice. She apologizes: she always has people meet her here because "When people see me talking to someone. They look." "People do say yes, at first... And then after a while they stop coming." Her smile holds a breath too long (her tell). Dusty resolves to be careful: he's known her three hours.
- "Let's stop apologizing to each other. And maybe have some tea."
- MAID SORREL: small, thin, slight, copper-red hair in a tight knot, PALE ICE-BLUE eyes, moves silently. Tea is over; the rule is the same for every student. Auriel pleads for a few minutes and is gently refused. Sorrel: "Tomorrow is a fresh day... perhaps this fine young gentleman could join you here again. Should he find his way a little faster." Dusty: "I'd like your company tomorrow." Auriel: tomorrow, four, here, "I'll... save the good cakes. The pink ones." She rushes off.
- Sorrel, alone with Dusty: "It's good to see someone talking to Miss Landsdon... I do wonder how long you'll last." "You'll learn. Like the rest of her so-called friends." Dusty steps in: "Could you be more specific, please." Sorrel, serene, a small cruel smile: "Trying to intimidate a Maid on your first day is not a very good idea." / "Maids are supposed to be neutral." / "We are. But we have eyes. And ears." Dusty steps back: "I'm sorry. I don't like people trying to scare me off." / "I wasn't... I was wondering if you would too." She ignores his follow-ups (why they stay away, who's telling them, the sash, her family) and leaves with the tray.
- Dusty's conclusion: Maids are people. The Maids' creed ("Beauty, Elegance, and Dignity above all else," which Rinnie relayed from Maedelyn) and the island's equality rule both bend for "the right ring, or the right apron." He doubts Valia can answer this item on the list.

13. SECOND DAY: MORNING, INTRO TO MAGIC, ALIGNMENT TESTING — POV Dusty (internal *** breaks)
- Bells at dawn. Dusty fell asleep at his desk studying his letters by lamplight ("ALIGNMENT had cost him most of an hour. He still wasn't sure of the G."). He starts to resent Valia over the tutor, then corrects himself: there's no meanness in her, she simply forgot. He remembers her rush ("you do need one, don't you, it's all right, lots of them do") and smiles.
- Breakfast on the move: two whole hot loaves eaten walking. Girls in lilac stare; a boy laughs. He ignores them.
- INTRO TO MAGIC (Brannoch): martial goes INTO THE BLOOD and never leaves the body (hence no glow). Elemental and healing work OUTSIDE the body: "Out. Always out." Dusty writes OUT and realizes his flame has never left him, never drained into Rinnie, and Brannoch said nothing about black haze or silver. He recalls Valia's "That's not how any of it—" and begins to believe his mana is different.
- MAGICAL APPLICATION: the sand pit is roped into three pens.
  - PROFESSOR STROUD (martial): human, past fifty, squat and square, iron-gray stubble hair, flattened crooked nose, tip of the left ear missing, scuffed leather jerkin. He keeps a weapons rack with the grain turned the same way and is deadly serious about weapons ("A spear is not a walking stick... In the north, a spear is the last friend you have in the world."). He wipes the shaft where a boy leaned on it.
  - VENN (elemental), center pen.
  - PROFESSOR TANTRIS (healing): OLD elf (the first old elf Dusty has seen), long brown hair going gray at the temples, clear blue eyes, fine lines around eyes and mouth, undyed cream wool robe with sleeves rolled. Patient and kind.
- Venn: "Go where you believe you belong. If you are wrong, you will be told." Dusty picks healing (about 30 there) to avoid lighting his fire in front of Venn.
- Tantris nicks his own finger with a small sleeve-knife: "Don't order it. Ask." Most fail and he sends them kindly to the other pens. A freckled girl (pale green) succeeds.
- The BULL-NECKED NOBLE (tight blazer, signet ring, gold glow) heals easily. Tantris suggests he also test elemental. The boy says Stroud already placed him in martial. Tantris, quiet and even: "You have as much potential for a martial alignment as I have for waking up one morning a human." He's built those shoulders with iron bars so his father sees a swordsman; "None of us chooses where we lean." The boy goes red and walks to Venn.
- Tantris calls Dusty over ("You. The tall one... It's open. Come on."). Dusty: "I'm sorry, sir. I've never done this before."
  - Step 1: imagine the mana already outside you, like wind across the brow. Dusty sends the black smoke of his flame up to brush his forehead. Tantris: "Oh, that's very good."
  - Step 2 (Tantris re-cuts his finger): bring it to the hand as paint, any color, a ball of color and wind, unrealized. Push it around the finger and give it its purpose. Dusty's comes up BLACK with a SILVER rim.
  - Dusty adds his own step: he pictures Rinnie coughing on the cot in the Greys, then healthy, laughing, running up the stairs of the honey-brick house. The mana changes into something that mends. Healed in seconds.
- Tantris: "Healer... Not a doubt in my mind." In passing, not suspicious: "That's a color I haven't seen in a few years. Lovely." Nobody else notices.
- Final counts: 20 healers, 60 elemental, 120 martial (ratio 1:3:6).
- Realization: most students are not the heroes of the soup priests' stories. They are wells or less, 17-18 years old, trying to hold a little light. Closing image: the crimson-blazer boy's vaunted fire is orange and "no bigger than a candle's."

14. HISTORY AND POTIONS — POV Dusty
- History blurs past again (the Treaty of Something, the burning of Somewhere).
